<title>USA: Puget Energy in salmon protection accord.</title>
<headline>Puget Energy in salmon protection accord.</headline>
<dateline>TACOMA, Wash. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Puget Sound Energy, Inc and the Puyallup Tribe announced Tuesday an agreement to protect salmon runs affected by the 26 megawatt Electron hydropower project on the Puyallup River.</p>
<p>The agreement calls for introducing new fishery stocks to the river and allowing upstream passage of the fish.</p>
<p>Construction will begin this fall on rearing ponds and downstream fish passage facilities will be constructed to enable the salmon to pass beyond the dam and powerhouse, the company said.</p>
<p>The agreement also provides for water to be released to the Puyallup River below the dam to help fish move down the river and migrate up the river.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
